---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

// The app's evening body check-in, in its own order (symetric-native
// src/lib/body/constants.ts, CHECKIN_BODY_DOMAIN_ORDER). End-of-day exhaustion
// is the required one, so it stays last here as it does in the app.
const bodyDomains = [
  "fatigue across the day",
  "joint and muscle pain",
  "widespread pain",
  "joint instability",
  "breathing (air hunger, breathless on effort, a tight chest)",
  "dizziness (lightheaded, heart racing, greying out on standing)",
  "gut (nausea, bloating, cramping)",
  "brain fog",
  "end-of-day exhaustion",
];

const bodyEvents = [
  "a joint going out",
  "nearly fainting",
  "a migraine starting",
  "a crash",
  "a reaction",
  "an injury or strain",
  "palpitations",
];

const mindDomains = [
  "mood",
  "energy",
  "anxiety",
  "concentration",
  "irritability",
  "social depletion",
  "sensory overwhelm",
  "motivation",
];

const tiers = [
  { name: "Mind", status: "Always on", on: true },
  { name: "Sleep", status: "Always on", on: true },
  { name: "Body", status: "Optional", on: false },
  { name: "Cycle", status: "Optional", on: false },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="symetric: What it tracks"
  description="Mind and sleep are the core, always on. Body and day-1 cycle logging are optional. Here's exactly what each one covers, and what symetric deliberately doesn't do."
>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="hero pb-tight tracks-hero">
      <div class="tracks-hero-text">
        <p class="kicker">What it tracks</p>
        <h1 style="max-width:20ch">Two things are always on. Two more are there if you need them.</h1>
        <p class="lede">symetric started as a mind tracker, and mind and sleep are still the core of what it does. Body and day-1 cycle logging are optional additions, for people who want more context alongside it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tier-glance" aria-label="The four things symetric can track, and whether each is always on or optional">
        {tiers.map((t) => (
          <div class="tier-row">
            <span class="tier-name">{t.name}</span>
            <span class={`tier-badge ${t.on ? "tier-badge--on" : "tier-badge--optional"}`}>{t.status}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ MIND + SLEEP (the core, paired) ============ -->
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="sec" aria-labelledby="core-h">
      <p class="sec-label">The core</p>
      <h2 id="core-h">Mind and sleep. Always on.</h2>
      <div class="core-pair mt-xl">
        <div>
          <h3>Mind</h3>
          <p class="mt-md muted">Where symetric started, and still the centre of what it does. 8 domains: {mindDomains.join(", ")}. <b>Pick 2 of them or all 8, and change your mind whenever you like.</b> Three check-ins a day by default, 30 seconds each, inside a window you set.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3>Sleep</h3>
          <p class="mt-md muted">Separate from the 8 domains, not something you switch on or off. Once a day: how did you sleep last night, and how many hours, if you want to log that part too, it&rsquo;s optional. <b>Skip it on the days you need to.</b></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="big-quiet mt-2xl muted">Most trackers make you choose: broad enough to cover everything that&rsquo;s going on, or simple enough to stick with. <b>You tell symetric what matters once, in under a minute, and it stays that light every day after</b>, however many domains you&rsquo;re tracking.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ BODY ============ -->
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="sec pt-tight" aria-labelledby="body-h">
      <p class="sec-label">Optional</p>
      <h2 id="body-h">Body.</h2>
      <p class="mt-lg muted"><b>If joint instability, standing up feeling faint, or persistent exhaustion are part of your picture</b>, alongside the mind side or instead of it, this is where that goes. Turn it on at signup or later in Settings.</p>
      <div class="plain mt-xl">
        <div class="line">
          <span class="tick yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <span class="txt"><b>{bodyDomains.length} domains you can check in on:</b> {bodyDomains.join(", ")}. End-of-day exhaustion is the one required question once body tracking is on, it asks each evening. Pick whichever of the rest apply to you. There&rsquo;s an optional morning check-in too, where you choose up to four of them to answer first thing.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="line">
          <span class="tick yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <span class="txt"><b>{bodyEvents.length} events you can log as they happen:</b> {bodyEvents.join(", ")}.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="line">
          <span class="tick yes" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
          <span class="txt"><b>Where it hurt, and what it felt like.</b> Mark pain or instability on a body map, and describe pain in words, aching, burning, shooting, because a 6 that aches and a 6 that burns aren&rsquo;t the same thing to a clinician.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-xl muted">Body tracking is newer than mind, and we&rsquo;re still refining it. Everything above works now, but expect it to keep changing.</p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ CYCLE ============ -->
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="sec pt-tight" aria-labelledby="cycle-h">
      <p class="sec-label">Optional, for context</p>
      <h2 id="cycle-h">Day 1. Nothing more.</h2>
      <p class="mt-lg muted">Log Day 1, the date your period starts, whenever it happens. That's the only thing you enter. From that, symetric shows a simple running count: Day 13, Day 24, however many days since your last Day 1. Log the next Day 1, and it resets.</p>
      <div class="cycle-callout mt-xl">
        <p>That&rsquo;s all it does. It doesn&rsquo;t predict your next period, estimate a phase, or draw conclusions from the date.</p>
        <p class="mt-md">Plenty of apps will tell you what phase you're probably in. symetric just tells you how many days it's been, so you and your clinician have that context, <b>not a guess dressed up as one</b>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <!-- ============ CLOSE ============ -->
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="close pt-tight" aria-labelledby="close-h">
      <h2 id="close-h">Start with mind. Add the rest if it helps.</h2>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <!-- TODO: real App Store and Google Play listing URLs not available yet -->
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#">Get symetric</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/report">Read the sample report</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
